---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';

import annulus from '../assets/illustrations/annulus.png';
import { codeTheme, gsapCode, standaloneCode } from '../content/examples';

import AnnulusVector from '../components/AnnulusVector.astro';
import RingFan from '../components/RingFan.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';

import '../styles/site.css';
import '../styles/scroll-story.css';
import '../styles/integration.css';

const repo = 'https://github.com/G0m1namm/domfx';
const setup = '/docs/installation';
const bindingCode = `// fire is an existing manual-clock attachment.
timeline.addLabel('ignite', 0.5);
const binding = bindFire(fire, timeline, {
  time: 4,
  intensity: 0.4,
  duration: 4,
  position: 'ignite',
});`;

---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="GPU edge effects for real HTML. Explore domfx on titles, links, SVGs, images, and cards while the original content stays interactive." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#14151B" />
    <title>domfx — Effects that follow your HTML</title>
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/CabinetGrotesk-Medium.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body id="top">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <div class="page-shell">
      <SiteHeader />

      <main id="main">
        <div class="scroll-story" id="scroll-story">
          <div class="story-scene">
            <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
              <div class="hero-copy">
                <h1 id="hero-title">Effects that follow<br />your HTML.</h1>
                <p class="lede">Add GPU effects to real elements.<br class="desktop-break" /> Your text stays selectable. Your links keep working.</p>
                <div class="actions">
                  <a class="primary-link" href="#examples">Try the live elements <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
                  <a class="text-link" href={setup}>Read the quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                </div>
                <p class="hero-note">Experimental & open source.</p>
                <p class="hero-instruction" id="toolbar-instruction" hidden>Scroll to explore. Use the controls to make it yours.</p>
                <noscript><p class="hero-note">JavaScript is off. Content, examples and setup links remain available.</p></noscript>
              </div>
              <RingFan live />
            </section>
            <section class="story-step image-step" id="examples" aria-labelledby="image-title">
              <h2 id="image-title" class="stage-title"><span class="reveal-line"><span>Every contour</span></span> <span class="reveal-line"><span>counts.</span></span></h2>
              <Image class="static-image" src={annulus} width={640} format="png" alt="Silver annular disc with an empty center" />
              <div class="stage-description"><p>The effect follows your image’s transparent silhouette, around the outside and through the opening in the middle.</p><p>Keep your original artwork. Adjust the fire without replacing the image.</p><a class="text-link" href="#example-svg">View the SVG ↗</a></div>
            </section>
            <section class="story-step vector-step" aria-labelledby="shape-title">
              <h2 id="shape-title" class="stage-title"><span class="reveal-line"><span>From pixels</span></span> <span class="reveal-line"><span>to paths.</span></span></h2>
              <div class="vector-host"><div class="vector-art" data-effect-host><AnnulusVector /></div></div>
              <div class="stage-description"><p>The same contour, now drawn in SVG. The effect follows its visible paths and preserves the space between them.</p><p>Image or vector, the original element stays on your page.</p><a class="text-link" href="#effect-heading">Try it on text ↓</a></div>
            </section>
            <section class="story-step text-step" aria-labelledby="effect-heading">
              <div class="text-host" data-effect-host><h2 id="effect-heading" data-effect-target>Keep the HTML.</h2></div>
              <p class="text-lede">The effect follows every letter.<br />Your text stays selectable.</p>
              <p class="selection-note">Select the heading, or use the controls to adjust the effect.</p>
            </section>
            <nav class="story-navigation" aria-label="Scroll story" hidden><a href="#example-image">Image</a><a href="#example-svg">SVG</a><a href="#effect-heading">Text</a></nav>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="integration-content">
          <section id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
            <div class="intro">
              <h2 id="features-title">Put Fire on<br />your timeline.</h2>
              <p>Bring the effect into the sequence you're already building. The optional <code class="package-name">@domfx/gsap</code> binding connects Fire's time and intensity to your timeline.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="grid">
              <article class="card timeline-card">
                <div class="card-heading">
                  <h3>Give it a cue.</h3>
                  <p>Add an entrance, place a label, then bring in Fire. One timeline keeps the sequence under your control.</p>
                </div>
                <figure class="timeline" aria-label="Example timeline: entrance from 0 to 0.5 seconds, then Fire at ignite for 4 seconds to 4.5 seconds.">
                  <div class="timeline-sheet">
                    <div class="ruler"><span>0s</span><span>0.5s</span><span>2.5s</span><span>4.5s</span></div>
                    <div class="lane"><span class="lane-label">Entrance</span><div class="lane-track"><div class="entrance"></div></div></div>
                    <div class="lane"><span class="lane-label">Fire</span><div class="lane-track"><div class="fire-range"><span>ignite</span><span>4 seconds</span><span>0.8 → 0.4</span></div></div></div>
                    <div class="timeline-key">ignite · inserted at 0.5s</div>
                  </div>
                  <figcaption>Example sequence: a 0.5-second entrance, followed by a 4-second Fire binding. Effect time moves to 4; intensity moves to 0.4.</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <div class="code-title"><strong>timeline.ts</strong><span>@domfx/gsap</span></div>
                <div class="integration-code-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Bind a manual Fire attachment to a GSAP timeline"><Code code={bindingCode} lang="ts" theme={codeTheme} /></div>
                <p class="code-note">Time and intensity interpolate linearly from their values at binding. Use the optional GSAP binding to coordinate the sequence.</p>
              </article>
              <article class="card settings">
                <div class="card-heading">
                  <h3>Set the character.</h3>
                  <p>Choose the initial settings when you attach Fire. Give the pattern, height and motion a deliberate starting point.</p>
                </div>
                <dl class="settings-list">
                  <div class="setting"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>0–1</dd><p>Set the effect's strength. This example starts at 0.8, then the timeline takes it to 0.4.</p><div class="measure" aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
                  <div class="setting"><dt>Flame height</dt><dd>8–64px</dd><p>Choose the height at creation. The shown configuration uses 32px.</p></div>
                  <div class="setting"><dt>Seed</dt><dd>314</dd><p>Fix the procedural pattern so you can work from a consistent starting point.</p></div>
                  <div class="setting"><dt>Clock</dt><dd>manual / ambient</dd><p>Use manual for timeline control. Choose ambient for a standalone effect that advances its own time.</p></div>
                  <div class="setting"><dt>Motion</dt><dd>respect</dd><p>The default respects reduced motion. Keep the original content available when the effect doesn't render.</p></div>
                </dl>
                <p class="source-note"><code>flameHeight</code> requires the current experimental source.</p>
              </article>
            </div>
            <article class="card controls" aria-labelledby="controls-title">
              <div><h3 id="controls-title">Your timeline.<br />Your controls.</h3><p>Use the GSAP methods you already know. The binding controls effect time and intensity; your timeline owns playback.</p></div>
              <div class="methods">
                <div class="method"><code>play() / pause()</code><p>Run or hold the sequence.</p></div>
                <div class="method"><code>seek() / reverse()</code><p>Visit a moment or play backward.</p></div>
                <div class="method"><code>timeScale()</code><p>Change the timeline's playback speed.</p></div>
                <div class="method"><code>repeat / yoyo</code><p>Configure these on the timeline.</p></div>
                <div class="method method-wide"><code>time · intensity · duration · position</code><p>Set the binding's destination, duration and insertion label. Use a label to place Fire alongside other animations.</p></div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </section>
          <section id="start" class="adoption" aria-labelledby="start-title">
            <div>
              <h2 id="start-title">Bring your own edge.</h2>
              <p>Start with one element and the motion you have in mind. Use the browser package on its own, or add the GSAP binding to fit Fire into your sequence.</p>
              <details class="details">
                <summary>See the complete GSAP setup</summary>
                <p class="disclosure-note">Run after mount, once fonts are ready. Provide your element as <code>target</code> and a positioned ancestor as <code>host</code>.</p>
                <div class="integration-code-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Full manual attachment and GSAP lifecycle example"><Code code={gsapCode} lang="ts" theme={codeTheme} /></div>
              </details>
              <details class="details">
                <summary>Prefer a standalone attachment?</summary>
                <p class="disclosure-note">The browser package doesn't need GSAP. With an ambient clock, Fire advances its own time.</p>
                <div class="integration-code-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Standalone ambient attachment example"><Code code={standaloneCode} lang="ts" theme={codeTheme} /></div>
              </details>
            </div>
            <div class="integration-start-action">
              <div data-effect-host><a id="scroll-target" data-effect-target class="primary" href={setup}>Read the quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
              <p class="start-note">Experimental and unpublished. The guide covers local tarball setup, standalone use and the optional GSAP binding.</p>
              <p class="start-note">WebGPU is required. Reduced motion or unavailable output leaves your original HTML in place.</p>
              <div class="secondary">
                <a href="/docs/support">Browser support ↗</a>
                <a href={`${repo}/tree/main/apps/lab`}>Inspect the lab ↗</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </main>
      <footer class="site-footer">
        <div class="footer-return"><div class="footer-callout"><h2>Make your HTML come alive.</h2><a class="text-link" href={setup}>Open the quickstart ↗</a></div><RingFan /></div>
        <div class="footer-grid">
          <div class="footer-brand"><a class="wordmark" href="#top">domfx<span aria-hidden="true">.</span></a><p>GPU effects for real HTML.</p><p class="footer-note">Experimental. Fire available today.<br />Package not published yet.</p></div>
          <nav aria-label="Explore"><h2>Explore</h2><a href="#examples">Examples</a><a href={setup}>Quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={repo}>Source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
          <nav aria-label="Resources"><h2>Resources</h2><a href="/docs/support">Browser support <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={`${repo}/tree/main/apps/lab`}>Diagnostic lab <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-bottom"><a href={`${repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT licensed <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="#top">Back to top <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span></a></div>
      </footer>
    </div>
    <p class="effect-notice" id="effect-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
    <aside class="effect-dock" id="playground" aria-label="Showcase controls" hidden>
      <section class="dock-panel" id="effect-panel" role="region" aria-labelledby="effect-title" hidden inert>
        <h2 class="dock-sr-only" id="effect-title">Effect</h2>
        <div class="control-row"><span id="effect-choice-label">Effect</span><fieldset id="effect-presets" aria-labelledby="effect-choice-label"><legend class="dock-sr-only">Available effects</legend><label><input type="radio" name="effect" value="none" /><span>None</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="effect" value="fire" checked /><span>Fire</span></label></fieldset></div>
        <div class="settings-fields">
          <div class="slider-row"><div class="value-row"><label for="effect-intensity" title="The scroll card peaks at this intensity. Other elements use it directly.">Intensity</label><label class="numeric-value"><input id="intensity-number" aria-label="Maximum intensity percent" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="70" /><span>%</span></label></div><input id="effect-intensity" aria-label="Maximum intensity" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="70" /><p class="dock-sr-only">The scroll card peaks at this value. Other targets use it directly.</p></div>
          <div class="slider-row"><div class="value-row"><label for="flame-height">Flame height</label><label class="numeric-value"><input id="height-number" aria-label="Flame height pixels" type="number" min="8" max="64" step="1" value="32" /><span>px</span></label></div><input id="flame-height" type="range" min="8" max="64" step="1" value="32" /></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="dock-panel" id="motion-panel" role="region" aria-labelledby="motion-title" hidden inert>
        <h2 class="dock-sr-only" id="motion-title">Motion</h2>
        <div class="settings-fields">
          <div class="slider-row"><div class="value-row"><label for="motion-speed">Speed</label><label class="numeric-value"><input id="speed-number" aria-label="Motion speed multiplier" type="number" min="0.1" max="2" step="0.1" value="1" /><span>×</span></label></div><input id="motion-speed" type="range" min="0.1" max="2" step="0.1" value="1" /></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span title="On repeats the selected range. Off runs continuously.">Range <span class="control-hint" aria-hidden="true">ⓘ</span></span><label class="segmented-switch"><span class="dock-sr-only">Repeat a range</span><input id="motion-loop" type="checkbox" role="switch" /><span class="switch-on" aria-hidden="true">On</span><span class="switch-off" aria-hidden="true">Off</span></label></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span title="Set the beginning and end of the repeated Fire time range, in seconds.">Start / end <span class="control-hint" aria-hidden="true">ⓘ</span></span><div class="motion-range"><input id="range-start" aria-label="Range start seconds" type="number" min="0" max="119.95" step="0.05" value="0" disabled /><div class="range-track"><input id="range-start-slider" aria-label="Range start slider" type="range" min="0" max="10" step="0.05" value="0" disabled /><input id="range-end-slider" aria-label="Range end slider" type="range" min="0" max="10" step="0.05" value="10" disabled /></div><input id="range-end" aria-label="Range end seconds" type="number" min="0.05" max="120" step="0.05" value="10" disabled /></div></div>
          <div class="control-row"><span title="System reduced motion always takes priority over this page setting.">Reduce motion <span class="control-hint" aria-hidden="true">ⓘ</span></span><label class="segmented-switch"><span class="dock-sr-only">Reduce motion on this page</span><input id="reduce-motion" type="checkbox" /><span class="switch-on" aria-hidden="true">On</span><span class="switch-off" aria-hidden="true">Off</span></label></div>
          <p class="dock-sr-only" id="system-motion">System motion preference is being checked.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="dock-panel prompt-panel" id="prompt-panel" role="region" aria-labelledby="prompt-title" hidden inert>
        <h2 class="dock-sr-only" id="prompt-title">Use it in your app</h2>
        <p id="prompt-summary"></p>
        <div class="prompt-target"><label for="prompt-target">Element</label><input id="prompt-target" type="text" maxlength="300" value="the main hero heading" /></div>
        <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Agent prompt"><code id="prompt-content"></code></pre>
        <div class="prompt-actions"><button class="primary-link" id="copy-prompt">Copy prompt</button><a class="text-link" href={setup}>Quickstart ↗</a></div>
        <p id="prompt-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </section>
      <div class="collapsed-bar">
        <div class="dock-controls">
          <button class="quiet-button" id="effect-settings" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="effect-panel" aria-label="Effect: Fire">Effect</button>
          <button class="quiet-button" id="motion-settings" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="motion-panel">Motion</button>
          <button class="quiet-button" id="view-prompt" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="prompt-panel">Prompt</button>
          <button class="quiet-button playback-button" id="effect-play" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Pause" title="Pause"><span class="playback-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span id="playback-label">Pause</span></button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
    <script src="../scripts/site.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
